  "note": "This sheet is RGB with no alpha channel, so it slices to one fused piece. That piece has been cut on its stated 20x1 grid, so the entries below are its cells in reading order - left to right, then top to bottom - one cell each and none of them annotated yet. Do not re-slice this sheet with apply=true: slicing finds the plate as one fused piece again and reports every cut cell as no longer found, so a re-slice discards the cut and anything authored onto it. Cut once, then annotate. 2172x724 as a 20x1 strip, so its cells are 109x724 - far from square, which the grid split handles. It already ships as a hand-written tileset built by art-source/tilesets/normalize_tilesets.py. Exporting over it would rewrite the ids and coordinates that GenMappingRegistry references, so treat this as a sheet to inspect or adopt deliberately, not to re-export casually. Note it loads as a sliced sheet addressed by frame index rather than as col/row doodads, so re-exporting it through this tool would change its shape in the registry, not just its coordinates.",
